WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.980
<i>One week has passed.</i>

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.900
<i>The library had more visitors than ever before.</i>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.780
<i>From the morning on,
it's now a social hub for students.</i>

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.070
<i>This will surely save it from being closed.</i>

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.750
<i>It's all thanks to the efforts
of Hose and the two girls.</i>

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.370
<i>And yet...</i>

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.720
EPISODE 12
THE ONE I LOVE IS...

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.800
Wow, the place is hopping.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.760
And we owe it all to Hose, right?
That guy's amazing.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.440
Yeah, at this rate,
I think the library will be safe. But...

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.440
Yeah. We figured there would be
a big influx of students like this.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:57.200
Sumireko, do you have any ideas
how to get even more people to come?

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.580
Well, um...

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.790
You two are as thick as thieves!

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.450
You make a good couple.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.790
Don't insinuate anything, you two!

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.250
S-Sorry, Sumireko.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.250
It's okay.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.170
<i>The other problem is ongoing,
with no end in sight.</i>

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.090
<i>I'd like to step in somehow...</i>

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>but we can't make a move.</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.800
<i>Because Cherry and Tsukimi
aren't doing anything wrong.</i>

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.520
I see.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.230
Next weekend, why don't you two—

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.060
Pansy!

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.940
Which shelf does this go on?

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.110
I-I'll show you.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.150
Sorry.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.860
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.570
Um, that book goes on this shelf.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.580
Oh, that's where it goes!

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.540
<i>But if I don't hurry up and do something...</i>

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.130
What?!

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.970
H-Hazuki has come to Nishikizuta
to help with the library?

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.010
What the heck is going on?

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.720
Calm down, freak-face.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.810
How can I calm down?

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.180
- What have I been trying so hard—
- I get it!

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.230
You wanted Pansy to have a boyfriend
and wanted to get into Toshobu High yourself

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.230
because you're in love with Hose, right?

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:21.160
I had Asunaro look into it, but you've
done a lot of things for the love of Hose.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.410
That includes last year's
regional tournament final.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.830
That's right!

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.620
That day, I knew Hazuki intended to meet with
Sanshokuin at the south exit, so I followed him.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.750
I was thinking that if luck were on my side,
I could profit from the situation.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:38.260
<i>So then she happened to see the exchange
between Sun-chan and Pansy.</i>

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.590
But it didn't work out.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:45.350
Even though I went as far
as wearing the same barrettes as Sanshokuin!

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:49.060
Just in case, I bought 100 spares!

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.270
<i>That's an over-abundance of caution!</i>

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.520
Since it's come to this,
please ask Sanshokuin out right now!

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.780
Forget it! In fact, you come to the library
and do something about—

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:04.330
I'm the manager of the baseball team,
so I don't have time for that after school.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.210
You're unexpectedly serious, huh?

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.580
Besides, it wouldn't do any good for me to go.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.260
It has to be you, Kisaragi,
since Sanshokuin is in love with you!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.140
Okay.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.550
I'll try to do something about Hose.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.270
Thank you!

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.850
Thank you so much!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.230
<i>Am I the only one who can do something?</i>

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.110
Well, I'll come again.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.190
Bye-bye!

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.070
That boy from Toshobu is so handsome.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.490
Yeah, I love his dazzling smile!

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.040
I'm glad we had
a lot of visitors again today, Joro.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.000
Yeah.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.370
Hey, Hose.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.750
What would you do if Pansy got a boyfriend?

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.630
Answer me. I want to know.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.220
I'd be sad...

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.680
but at a time like that,
"Congratulations" is the only thing I could say.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.640
I see. Got it.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.100
But why do you ask?

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.900
Pansy, I need to talk to you.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.610
Oh, good timing.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.440
I have something to tell you, too.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.240
You, too?

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.070
Yes.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:30.740
Actually, Sun-chan and I
have an agreement to start dating.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.040
S-Sumireko, what'd you just say?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.260
A little while ago, Sun-chan asked me...

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.760
<i>Nothing. Just talking to myself.</i>

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.050
<i>Listen, Pansy.</i>

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:53.230
<i>If Nishikizuta High
goes to Koushien this year...</i>

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.480
<i>I want you to be my girlfriend.</i>

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.440
I agreed to that.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.200
I don't believe it! Sumirekocchi!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.660
It's true, Sakurabara.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.990
But that...

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.290
Hosecchi.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.590
Um...

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.840
I-I see. Good.
Congratulations, Sumireko.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.550
Thank you.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.430
And finally, Joro.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:32.890
Wh-What?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:37.270
I'm not so strong
that I can be devoted to someone

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.310
who never pays me any attention.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.030
So would you stay away
from the library for a while?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.940
You're more trouble than you're worth.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:46.610
Pansy!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.700
That's mean!
Joro didn't do anything wrong!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:52.700
But it's the truth, isn't it?
He couldn't do anything this whole week.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.620
Nothing about the library
and nothing about the other thing.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.080
Having someone like that around
is just an annoyance.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.670
Okay.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.050
I won't come here anymore.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.300
Joro!

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.800
President Cosmos, Himawari, Asunaro,

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.600
I'll let you handle the rest.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.760
Joro.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.860
SORRY SUN-CHAN...
AFTER YOU'RE DONE WITH YOUR CLUB,
CAN YOU MEET ME IN CLASS?

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.690
Joro, what's wrong?

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.490
Did something happen at the library?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.740
You look miserable.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.160
Um...

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.410
Did you hear that Pansy
promised to be my girlfriend?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.920
I...

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:44.170
You called me here because you wanted
to hear me say it, right?

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.920
Yeah, but, um...

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.680
Wait, I get it! It was your plan, right?
To solve the current situation.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.800
Dummy!

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.390
I've been a good best friend, right?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:59.190
Whenever you were in trouble,
I would always be there to help.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.940
It's like our roles were reversed from before.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:12.280
But if I hadn't done that, I wouldn't have
been able to spend time with Pansy.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.370
Then, Sun-chan, all this time...

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.620
I really am grateful to Hose.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:23.290
Thanks to him, it looks like the library
will be saved and Pansy will be mine.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.130
Well, I'm still counting on you.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.510
I did what I was supposed to do.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.760
So now you do what you're supposed to do...

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.470
as my best friend.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:40.270
As your best friend?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.360
Yeah, as my best friend.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.570
Yeah.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:52.910
All right! Well, I'm going to take off.
See you tomorrow.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.120
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.950
I see.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.410
CHEERFUL SKEWERS

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.250
Welcome!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.750
Sasanqua, here we go!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.170
<i>Summer vacation.</i>

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.760
<i>I haven't been back
to the library since that day.</i>

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.470
<i>But it's better this way.</i>

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.930
<i>After all, I'm still surrounded
by my cute childhood friend,</i>

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.390
<i>the beautiful president of the student council,</i>

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.850
<i>and cheerful classmates.</i>

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:28.900
<i>Isn't this my ideal situation?</i>

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.990
<i>So as for her...</i>

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.030
U-Um, Joro.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.200
About the library...

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:39.580
The goal was achieved,
so it seems like it can stay open.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.460
Oh, really? That's good.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:48.630
- Um, it's thanks to you, Joro. Because of you—
- No. Come on.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.880
It's thanks to Hose.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.090
But we need you, Joro!

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.390
Without you around, Pansy is...

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.100
She doesn't need me.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.680
She's got a guy who's more dependable.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.190
Sorry. I have to get back to work.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.860
Joro!

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.490
- Joro, good work today.
- Thanks.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.870
By the way,
you're not going back to the library?

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.080
Th-That came out of the blue!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.620
I'm just a little curious.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.210
It's not like I'm needed anymore.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.630
Only you.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.420
You're the only one who can save Pansy
from Hose and those girls.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:37.640
No, Sun-chan solved that problem with
his agreement for her to be his girlfriend—

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:43.180
Is Hose someone who would give up
just because the person he likes has a boyfriend?

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.270
Still, I'm out of the picture!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:53.110
Joro. If you want to help Pansy... no...

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:57.570
If you want to be with her,
there's still something you should do.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.780
Something I should do?

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:05.370
Think about what Sun-chan told you
one more time.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.290
<i>I did what I was supposed to do.</i>

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.920
<i>So now you do what you're supposed to do...</i>

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.260
<i>as my best friend.</i>

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.090
Don't tell me that agreement was...

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.300
But it's beyond me.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.930
That's not true.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.350
I can't do it!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.350
I can't stop Hose!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.310
Pansy told me to stay away
from the library for a while...

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.730
Wait. Why "for a while"?

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.110
Not forever.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.400
That's...

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.910
You finally realized?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.490
That's right. Pansy was protecting you.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:49.160
You, the one
who was most caught up in her problem.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.540
She just left behind a small SOS.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.510
<i>That girl!</i>

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:00.090
<i>M-Me, too. I'll try to do my best
in my own way.</i>

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:04.010
<i>I can't let you do all the work, Joro.</i>

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.100
<i>Right. I'm counting on you.</i>

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.310
So what do you want to do, Joro?

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.270
It's obvious.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.030
I'm going to help Pansy.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.990
You're not honest, are you?

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.820
So what do I do?

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.160
I understand her message,
but taking measures—

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.450
Huh? Wh-What a coincidence.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.540
Running into you here...

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.670
Coincidence? I work here.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.210
What are you doing here, Sasanqua?

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.720
Recently, you haven't been a creep at all!

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.050
Excuse me?

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.300
If something's happened...

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.510
tell me about it!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.930
Even I can give you a little support—

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.190
- Wait. What are you making me say?
- Sorry!

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.150
A-Anyway...

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.360
O-Oh, um, lately things
haven't been going well for me.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.150
You go, Sasanqua!

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:04.530
Do you have a precedent
where something did go well for you?

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.570
She finally went for it!

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.070
Yeah! She's so cute!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:05.950
Well...

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:05.950
Go get him!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.700
That doesn't matter!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.160
You should just act like your usual self!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.210
<i>Act like my usual self.</i>

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.340
I see.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.590
You're right.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.600
There's that creepy smile.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.600
Yep. Thanks, Sasanqua.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.890
I'm glad.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.600
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.310
It's not like I came here to see you!

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.770
I was already in the neighborhood.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.020
That's what I figured.

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.150
W-Well, see you around.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:40.990
Yeah.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:45.110
All right, now to think
of a plan that's up my alley.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.240
Sweet!

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.200
Iced cocoa.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.620
I'm an idiot, such an idiot!

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.620
Yes. You're in love.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:58.920
Yo, Joro.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.130
What's up?

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.550
I'm glad you guys
are on a winning streak with regionals.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.890
Thank you. At this rate,
we'll go all the way to the finals!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.720
So is that all you wanted to say to me?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.310
No, that wasn't it. Um...

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.900
I'm sorry! I don't think
I can cheer you on at this year's finals!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.570
Something more important has come up!

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:25.650
Huh? More important than your best friend?

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.660
More important than you,
my best friend, Sun-chan.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.200
I'm sorry. I figured it out.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.540
I figured it all out.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.710
I'm really sorry!

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.670
The team just has to win.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.340
Hey, Joro.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:46.630
Bottom of the ninth, one out, a man on third.
The score is tied.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.140
One run in, and we win.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:53.890
At a time like that,
what do you think the batter should do?

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.140
The pitcher for the other side has a real arm,

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:00.360
so it's not going to be easy getting
a hit off of him, let alone a home run.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:01.980
So what do you do?

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:06.990
In that situation,
there's only one thing you should do.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.570
If you can answer that, then I'm relieved.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:17.540
I'm the batter, and you're the runner on third.
All there is to it.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.130
Thank you for the help again today.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:25.090
I really appreciate you coming all this way,
even after we've achieved our goal.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.590
Oh, this is nothing! Right, Tsukimicchi?

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.050
We'll do our best until the end.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:34.770
Well, I'll be heading out now.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.680
Wait, Sumireko!

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.270
What is it?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.560
I really like you.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.610
So I want you to be my girlfriend!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:49.740
I-I apologize for blurting it out,
but I just had to tell you.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.160
But Sun-chan and I...

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.200
Yeah. I know.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.950
But that's only if they win at regionals, right?

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:01.380
So if they don't,
I want you to think about me, too.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.130
Listen, you don't have to—

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.880
Sounds good to me, Sumirekocchi!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.300
He just wants you to think about it.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.470
No!

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:09.760
After all...

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.890
Think about Hose's feelings. Please.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.390
I-I...

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.730
As I predicted.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:27.400
With me out of the way,
you guys are living it up.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:29.490
Joro!

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.950
Joro!

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.910
What did you come here for?

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:35.160
- I told you to stay away for a while—
- And...

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.790
I did stay away for a while, didn't I?

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.170
Y-You're a nuisance, so go—

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.380
Hey, Pansy.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.960
Do you know what a "woman's privilege" is?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.050
You don't know? Then I'll tell you.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:52.800
NATSUME SOUSEKI
HAND-WRITTEN ESSAY
KOKORO

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.800
A "woman's privilege"...

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:57.010
is you selfishly indulging yourself
in manipulating me!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:03.520
You're a completely spoiled child
who gets lonely easily, right?

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.560
THE TORTOISE AND THE HARE

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.360
Um, Joro, what's going on?

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.070
It's been a while, so I'm glad to see you, but...

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:18.040
Hose, I challenge you.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.040
- Challenge?
- Yeah.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.500
Actually, I'm in the middle
of something important with Sumireko.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.130
Jorocchi! Can't it wait?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.840
Joro, this is a library,
so why don't you be quiet?

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.090
<i>Figures Cherry and Tsukimi
are running interference for him.</i>

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:39.180
I-I want to hear what Joro has to say.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.640
Pansy, you...

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.350
This is...

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.610
This is a lot of trouble.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.400
NATSUME SOUSEKI
HAND-WRITTEN ESSAY
KOKORO

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.400
Right now, I've got nothing but free time.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.860
Um...

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.910
Hose, listen to what I have to say first.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.080
You heard what Pansy said.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.950
Besides, we're friends, aren't we?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.750
Well, when you put it that way...

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.080
okay.

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:07.960
I'll take that to mean you accept my challenge.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.630
There's a bit of a punishment
for the loser, though.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:15.680
Of course I'm in! You asked me as a friend.
I could never say no to that.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:20.680
Glad to hear it! Then I'll start
by explaining the punishment aspect.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.850
<i>No matter what happens, he'll never give up.</i>

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:26.440
<i>That's why...</i>

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:32.070
Whoever loses has to stay away
from Sumireko Sanshokuin

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.280
and can't even talk to her.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.740
<i>I have to physically crush him!</i>

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.870
Now for the challenge.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:45.120
Wait a second! I didn't know
the punishment would involve Sumireko!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:48.920
I already told you.
The punishment is part and parcel of it.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.340
B-But...

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.090
Hey, Hose...

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.180
you did agree to the challenge, right?

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:58.340
Did you have your fingers crossed
or something?

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:01.560
If so, any promise you made
to Pansy going forward, for example,

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:04.230
would be immediately suspect, you know?

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.060
Wh-Why are you doing this, Joro?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.440
Aren't we friends?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:12.940
Yes, that's right!
You're absolutely right. You're my friend.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.360
We're like kindred spirits!

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:19.280
Then let's call off this challenge and talk it out.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.320
I won't let you...

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.990
Won't let me... what?

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.670
I'm saying that
I won't let you have Sumireko Sanshokuin!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.090
Okay, Joro.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.600
If you want to go there,
we'll have a fair-and-square challenge!

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:48.350
Fair and square? That's just like you.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.020
Then I'll explain the rules.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:54.230
First, these will be used for the challenge.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.030
Sumireko wears those.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.240
I've got an acquaintance
who has a ton of them.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.070
I borrowed them from her.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.950
How do the barrettes fit in?

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:05.700
It's not that difficult.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.200
So first...

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:09.460
Here. Here. Here.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.630
Each girl holding a barrette
gives it to either you or me,

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:16.760
whoever they think should be with Pansy.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.510
The person who has the most barrettes
at the end is the winner.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:21.970
In other words, it's like a popularity contest.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:25.220
It'll take place at the final game
of the regional tournament,

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.350
at the ballpark where the game is held.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.230
The reason for it being there is simple.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:34.820
If we did it right now, with six votes,
there's a possibility of a tie, so...

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.150
So?

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:39.990
At the final game,
if Nishikizuta wins, I get an extra barrette.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:45.160
If Toshobu wins, you get an extra barrette.
I added that rule.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:49.500
Well, if our teams don't make it
to the final game, we can rethink it then.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.410
So—

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:52.170
That's a terrible challenge!

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:55.000
Hose doesn't have a chance to win it.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.420
Oh, really?

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:59.130
That's right! After all,
the ones with the barrettes are—

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.300
- It's okay, you two.
- But...

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:04.390
Whatever the challenge,
I swear I won't lose it!

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:05.720
Leave it to me!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.520
<i>Fish!</i>

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:12.650
<i>And so, this is how Amatsuyu Kisaragi
hooks the main character role!</i>

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.690
<i>I mean, I decided
on the terms of the challenge.</i>

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.610
<i>So of course the outcome is tilted in my favor!</i>

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:24.910
<i>The girls with barrettes are Pansy, Cosmos,
Himawari, Asunaro, Cherry, and Tsukimi.</i>

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.450
<i>In other words, more than half are on my side!</i>

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.370
<i>I've as good as won!</i>

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.500
A serious fight?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:34.880
Ridiculous. I could never win that.

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:37.130
I'm going to be myself
and win in an underhanded way!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.710
I'm a naughty boy!

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.670
Jorocchi, you're a traitor!

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.800
Yes, what about it?

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.220
You're scum.

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:47.260
I get that all the time!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:51.100
I don't think Hose has a disadvantage.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:52.810
If anything, he's got the advantage, no?

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.140
Cosmoscchi!

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.980
Joro, I have one favor to ask.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:59.730
You said you want the vote
to be at the final game,

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:02.950
but can I give my barrette right now?

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.280
Joro, me, too!

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.110
Me, too.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.990
Okay, but only you three.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:13.710
<i>If I won it here, I'd feel bad for him,
so I'll limit it to three early votes.</i>

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.000
<i>I'm such a nice guy!</i>

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.420
I appreciated your point
about a woman's privilege.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.880
So I might be selfish and unreasonable...

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.300
But the rest is up to you.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.880
That's where we stand.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.300
H-Huh?

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.720
You three are acting weird.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:31.560
No way!

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:32.770
Here, Hose.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.850
You can have mine, too, Hose.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.520
Here you go, Hose.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.020
<i>Wait a second!</i>

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.480
<i>The opening was just playing,
with even the credits!</i>

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:44.070
<i>Any way you slice it,
that means I win a sweeping victory!</i>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.660
<i>All I did was act like a main character!</i>

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.160
E-Everyone...

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:49.620
thank you!

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.080
Thank you!

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.580
Thank you!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:58.170
Even Shuka Saito betrayed me!

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.170
- I don't believe it.
- Why?

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:05.300
Cherry, do you remember
what you two told us before?

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.380
What we told you?

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:10.550
Tsukimi, it's difficult for friendship
and love to coexist, right?

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.600
But I want both!

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:14.930
Both? What do you mean?

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:17.730
I'm Pansy's friend...

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:21.190
but also a rival, so...

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.110
Are you three...

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.030
I'm not interested
in being anything but number one.

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:29.200
I hate the idea of being a runner-up!

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:31.370
I won't let anybody else have the top headline!

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:33.540
Um, everyone...

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:36.210
So I'm going to come clean...

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:37.870
About my true feelings...

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:38.710
For you, Joro!

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:40.170
Joro!

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:42.710
I love you so much, it makes me crazy!

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:44.510
I want to be your woman!

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:46.010
I love you, Joro!

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:48.220
I want to be your girlfriend!

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:52.300
Please let me be with you forevermore
as your sweetheart!

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:56.640
<i>I'm totally thrilled, but the timing is...</i>

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:00.270
You're not my friends for nothing.

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:02.860
Joro, hang in there.

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:05.990
All right! I'm going to do this!

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:08.700
I'm going to settle this
and tie up all the loose ends!

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:11.620
Joro, you're not my friend anymore.

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:14.330
I won't let anyone else have Sumireko!

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.580
I finally got to see you!
And I won't let go of our bond ever again!

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:22.210
Lines worthy of a romcom protagonist!

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:25.210
But I'm going to be the one who wins!

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:27.380
Don't think the main character always wins!

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:29.550
People have had their fill of that kind of story!

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:34.970
So I'm going to leave
all romantic comedies in the dust!

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.640
THE END

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.730
It ain't over yet!
We've got a little more story left!
